From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] OpenGL: SDL_GL_LoadLibrary holds the library already loaded

SDL 1.2 holds the OpenGL library from SDL_GL_LoadLibrary until SDL_Quit.
Here, when SDL 2 has one loaded already (a window made before: an
SDL_OPENGL one, or one the GL renderer draws, as for a splash screen),
SDL_GL_LoadLibrary answered "already loaded" and took no reference; the
program looked its GL functions up, SDL_SetVideoMode destroyed that
window, SDL 2 unloaded the library with it and loaded it again for the
new one, at another address. Unreal Tournament 2004's first glGetString
then called into nothing (SIGSEGV in UOpenGLRenderDevice::SetRes).
Take a reference to the library loaded instead (SDL_GL_LoadLibrary(NULL)
of SDL 2 counts one more).

Upstream: not yet
Signed-off-by: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/SDL12_compat.c
+++ b/src/SDL12_compat.c
@@ -8390,7 +8390,13 @@
         char *dup;
 
         if (SDL20_strcmp(err, "OpenGL library already loaded") == 0) {
-            return 0;
+            /* ...but hold a reference to the one loaded, as SDL 1.2 holds
+               its library until SDL_Quit: it may be the library of a window
+               made before (an SDL_OPENGL window, or one drawn by the GL
+               renderer) that SDL_SetVideoMode destroys, and SDL 2 unloads it
+               with its last window. The program's GL function pointers,
+               looked up in between, would then point into nothing. */
+            return SDL20_GL_LoadLibrary(NULL);
         }
         /* reset the actual error. */
         dup = SDL20_strdup(err);
